      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing a Dead-Letter Queue**\n\nI'm focusing now on selecting an external provider for the dead-letter queue functionality. I'm leaning toward AWS SQS because it's a common and well-defined option for this. The next step is to make this choice explicit in the Python code itself.\n\n\n**Defining the File Structure**\n\nNow, I'm defining the basic structure for `dead_letter.py`. I'm going to import `boto3`, then create a function named `send_to_dead_letter_queue` that takes a message and the queue URL. Inside the function, an SQS client will be established using `boto3.client('sqs')`. I'll set up the function to use the client to send the messages. I'm leaving a placeholder for the concrete AWS SQS queue URL for later. I plan to start by creating this initial file content.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789887196503,
          "start": 1789887193290
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bd9720ca001WnWJD18Pqbygm6",
      "message_id": "msg_0bd971b3b001qoiLHC7DcEVCHS",
      "session_id": "ses_f4268e4d2ffeV709SEBSU51LJf",
      "time_created": 1789887193290,
      "time_updated": 1789887196504
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "r47gOLkkKjvDU0KW",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\nimport os\n\ndef send_to_dead_letter_queue(message_body: str, queue_url: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sends a failed message to a dead-letter queue using AWS SQS.\n\n    Args:\n        message_body: The content of the failed message.\n        queue_url: The URL of the AWS SQS dead-letter queue.\n    \"\"\"\n    sqs_client = boto3.client(\n        'sqs',\n        region_name=os.environ.get('AWS_REGION', 'us-east-1'),  # Make region configurable\n        aws_access_key_id=os.environ.get('AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID'),\n        aws_secret_access_key=os.environ.get('AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY')\n    )\n\n    try:\n        response = sqs_client.send_message(\n            QueueUrl=queue_url,\n            MessageBody=message_body\n        )\n        print(f\"Message sent to dead-letter queue: {response['MessageId']}\")\n        return response\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error sending message to dead-letter queue: {e}\")\n        raise\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    # Example usage (replace with your actual dead-letter queue URL)\n    DEAD_LETTER_QUEUE_URL = os.environ.get(\"DEAD_LETTER_QUEUE_URL\", \"YOUR_AWS_SQS_DEAD_LETTER_QUEUE_URL\")\n    if DEAD_LETTER_QUEUE_URL == \"YOUR_AWS_SQS_DEAD_LETTER_QUEUE_URL\":\n        print(\"WARNING: Please set the DEAD_LETTER_QUEUE_URL environment variable or replace the placeholder in dead_letter.py\")\n    else:\n        failed_message = \"This is a failed message that needs to be processed later.\"\n        send_to_dead_letter_queue(failed_message, DEAD_LETTER_QUEUE_URL)\n",
            "filePath": "dead_letter.py"
          },
