        "text": "**Defining External Provider**\n\nI've just finished the `dead_letter.py` file. It leverages `boto3` to interact with AWS SQS. The provider, in this case, is clearly identified within the code via `import boto3` and the instantiation of `boto3.client('sqs')`. I believe the integration is now complete, but I plan to review edge cases for robustness.\n\n\n**Confirming Dependency Identification**\n\nI've confirmed the external provider identification. The `dead_letter.py` script distinctly uses `boto3` to interface with AWS SQS. The inclusion of `import boto3` and `boto3.client('sqs')` unequivocally pinpoints the dependency. Placeholders for credentials and the region, plus the example usage, further clarify the reliance on an external system. I'm satisfied that this fulfills all requirements.\n\n\n",
